course: dictionary
lesson: 245
title: Alongside: next to or together with
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Alongside is a useful little word with two meanings. First, it means next to, beside or along the side of something. «The boat sailed alongside the pier.» The boat is right by the side of the pier.
explain: Second, it means together with someone, working or being with them. «Ella worked alongside her partner on the science project.» Ella and her partner were doing the work side by side, as a team.
explain: To check, swap in beside or together with. If the sentence still makes sense, you have the right meaning. «Pigeons have lived beside people for thousands of years» still makes sense, so alongside means beside here.
fact: Alongside means next to, beside or along the side of something.
fact: Alongside also means together with someone, working or being with them.
fact: «Alongside» can come before a noun, as in «alongside the dinosaurs» or «alongside people».
fact: Some words, like alongside, can work in more than one way. Look at the sentence to see which meaning fits.
fact: «Alongside» can also be used as an adverb, as in «The boat came alongside»: it moved to the side of something.
exercise: «The boat sailed alongside the pier.» What does alongside mean here? | Inside the pier | Under the pier | Far away from the pier | *Right beside the pier
exercise: «Ella worked alongside her partner on the science project.» What does alongside mean here? | Far away from her partner | Against her partner | Instead of her partner | *Together with her partner
exercise: «Pigeons have lived alongside people for thousands of years.» What does alongside suggest? | Hiding from people | Flying away from people | *Living near people, together with them | Fighting people for a long time
test: «Wolves began living alongside people more than 15,000 years ago.» Which word could replace alongside without changing the meaning? | Apart from | Against | Before | *Together with
test: Mia says alongside means far away. Is she right? | Yes, it means under | *No, it means next to or together with | No, it means very quickly | Yes, it means far away from
exam: What is the best way to check the meaning of alongside in a sentence? | Skip it and never read the sentence again | Look only at the first word of the sentence | Count the letters in the word | *Swap in beside or together with and see if the sentence still makes sense
